WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.133
-Hello.
-You look gorgeous.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.601
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.434
-Thank you for having me.
It's always my favorite.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.467
-I love that you're here

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:07.501
and I love that you come
on our show.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:08.968
And I'm so -- I want to say --

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.567
I want to say congratulations
to you, you're newly engaged.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:14.033
-I sure am.
-Come on.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.334
-Whoa!
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.567
-Yes.
-Now, how was --

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:19.567
Tell me about the proposal.
Was it a surprise?

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.567
Was it planned?

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:21.767
-I secured the rock.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.133
My work here is finished.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:26.067
-Yes! You did it!
-I will just let myself go now.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:30.434
No, um, well, I -- I wasn't
necessarily surprised

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.367
because I was like,
"Listen, you know,

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:35.868
I'm out here on the streets.
You gotta lock it down."

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.501
-Okay.
-I was like, dropping hints

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.734
left and right.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.968
I was like, "Babe, wow my nails
look so good."

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:45.100
And we went to Mexico
for the holidays

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.567
and he, I guess, set up
this whole grand thing

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.400
and then that fell through.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.834
And so, on Christmas Eve,
he was setting up this dinner

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:57.467
on the balcony, but I thought
it was Christmas Eve dinner,

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:01.367
because I thought Christmas Eve
was reserved for baby Jesus.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.367
So that was, I was like,
"Oh no, I --

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.100
it's probably not going to
happen tonight,"

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.400
and then it sure did.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.100
-Wow.
-It sure did.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.267
-You shared the evening
with baby Jesus.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.400
-With tiny baby Jesus.
-Yes.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.234
And -- [laughs] and you had
this beautiful dinner

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:15.634
and you go,
"Yeah, it's just perfect.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.334
-It was amazing.
I'm so happy.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:20.200
-And you told me that the ring
is very extra special to you.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.234
Why?
-Yeah, so he worked

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:26.968
with this Vietnamese,
family-owned jeweler

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:29.434
from Canada -- Paris Jewelers --
to make it,

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:34.968
and he knows how
important my heritage is to me.

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:37.934
And he knows that paying
it forward

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.367
means a lot to me, as well.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.734
And so, he worked with
these beautiful ladies there,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:46.667
and I'm -- I'm so happy and
I -- Yeah, I can't believe it.

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.934
-I'm so happy to see that.
This is great.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:53.067
-How did you first meet?

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:57.300
-Well, we met at an Emmy party,
and I slid in,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.267
I got his digits, and I --
as we were leaving I was like,

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:06.033
"Oh, hey, hey, hey.
Um, I thought of this joke,

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.734
but I forgot the punch line.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:13.067
Can I have your number, and then
when I remember it later on,

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.501
I'll just text you."

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.634
And so that's how I got, yes --
-Wow, that's a good move.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.033
-A smooth criminal.

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:22.267
And, yeah, so then I texted him
like 30 minutes later,

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.901
and I said, "Well, well, okay.

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:28.267
What do you call
a pile of kittens?"

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.234
-What do you call
a pile of kittens?

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:31.734
-A meow-ntain.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.501
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.200
-A meow --
-A meow-ntain.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.367
-A meow-ntain.
-And that's how you get

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.834
a fiance.
-There you go.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:39.467
And that's exactly right.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.701
It worked out perfect.

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:44.734
You know, it is Nana Week
here at the show.

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:46.400
Would you like to give
a shout-out to your grandma?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.100
-Yes, my grandma loves
your show.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.567
Um, so, hi, Grandma.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.968
-Hi, Grandma!
-Look, it's my friend.

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:54.968
-Look, Lana is doing great,
Grandma.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:57.367
-Thank you.
-We're giving you a big hug.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.100
That's so good.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.701
I wanna talk about your movie,
"Moonshot."

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:01.934
-"Moonshot." Oh, oh!

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.601
Cole really wishes he was here.

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:04.701
He sends his love.
-The funniest --

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.200
-He's the best.
-I love Cole Sprouse.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.467
-Yes, he's awesome.

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:08.968
-He is a fun human being.

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:11.367
-It -- honestly? It was so much
fun to work with him.

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.133
It felt like --
we shot it last summer --

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.801
it felt just like we were at,
like, daycare, weirdly,

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.701
like, all --
every single day on set,

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.367
because we were always just
having so much fun,

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.734
and it's about basically
these two people

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.167
who are stuck in a spaceship
together,

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.501
traveling through space and time
to get to their loved ones.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:28.834
So it's, like,
an adventure rom-com,

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.100
but, like, that's I feel like
not even a genre.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.067
Like a feel, like, that's, like,
such a niche.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.434
-You're starting a new genre.

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:37.200
-Like a sci-fi, weird, rom-com
is what it is.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.601
So if that's your thing,
watch it.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:39.968
-It's a sci-fi rom-com.
-Yeah.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.334
-Yeah, this is brand new.
No one's seen anything like it.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.634
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:46.133
Here's Lana Condor
and Cole Sprouse in "Moonshot."

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:47.133
Take a look at this.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:52.033
♪♪

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.968
-Initiating
ambient sound control.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.400
♪♪

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.400
-Hey, you cannot
under any circumstances

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.601
leave my room, okay?

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.267
-What?
-I will sneak you in food,

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:05.167
there's a bathroom,
it'll be like...camping.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.100
-Okay, clearly, you've never
gone camping before.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.868
And I -- I'm not going to spend
my first trip

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:10.501
through space on the toilet.

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.501
-Because you prefer
the air ducts?

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.734
-Because what do you think
happens when two people

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.367
are trapped in the same room
together?

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:19.100
-When two humans are confined
for an extended period,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:22.701
it results in either
more humans or fewer humans.

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:23.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:25.400
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.534
-Well done.
Lana Condor, everybody.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:31.067
"Moonshot" begins streaming
this Thursday on HBO Max.

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:32.234
We love you.

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:33.367
-Thank you for coming.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.634
-Congratulations. So happy.
-Thank you.

